WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.550
Check yourself with two questions
from the module's knowledge check.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:07.120
First: what happens when an
issuing certificate authority

3
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.325
in the trust store has no
revocation list configured?

4
00:00:10.325 --> 00:00:11.288
The answer is b.

5
00:00:11.288 --> 00:00:13.937
Entra doesn't check revocation for that

6
00:00:13.937 --> 00:00:16.987
authority's certificates,
which is rule C B one.

7
00:00:16.987 --> 00:00:20.894
Second: an eighteen and
a half million byte list

8
00:00:20.894 --> 00:00:24.300
raises C B five for GCC
but not for GCC High.

9
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:24.988
Why?

10
00:00:24.988 --> 00:00:25.997
The answer is b.

11
00:00:25.997 --> 00:00:30.453
C B five warns at eighty percent
of the cloud's interactive limit,

12
00:00:30.453 --> 00:00:35.750
and GCC High's limit is forty-five megabytes,
so the same size is under the line.

13
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:40.680
The module page has two more questions,
each linked to the section that teaches it.
